:{{DIcon|Разговор}} Listen
:'''Complaining Miner:''' I told Antonia from the beginning: We never should have let those vagrants mine with us. I wouldn't be in this mess if it weren't for those thugs.
:'''Upright Miner:''' Enough already. Nobody has it easy &mdash; this is a time to help each other out.
:'''Upright Miner:''' I remember one of your uncles had to flee Rivet Town, which makes him a vagrant too, right? Would you drive him away?
:'''Complaining Miner:''' ...He's family. The other vagrants aren't my problem.

:{{DIcon|Разговор}} Listen
:'''Worried Wife:''' Have any of you seen my husband? He's a good-looking guy &mdash; tall and thin...
:'''Wildfire Member Caring for the Injured:''' You again? Quit joking around! No need to add to the confusion.
:'''Worried Wife:''' *sigh* You think I'm joking? I saw you taking down the names of the miners &mdash; that's why I came over.
:'''Wildfire Member Caring for the Injured:''' Oh... You can put the name down here.

:{{DIcon|Разговор}} Listen
:'''Concerned Miner:''' Peak... he's done for. He was asleep in there.
:'''Exhausted Miner:''' Easy, Dr. Natasha told you to rest. What if your wound opens up again? Besides, Elaine will get him out, she's a reliable girl.
:'''Concerned Miner:''' Elaine was in there too!? Quick, we have to&mdash;
:'''Exhausted Miner:''' Calm down and stop worrying. Wildfire's already gone in.

:{{DIcon|Разговор}} Listen
:'''Bullheaded Vagrant:''' Don't come any closer! The road's blocked &mdash; stay where you are!
:'''Anxious Miner:''' ...Whoa, easy! Why are you hiding in there? Don't you know what happened in the mine?
:'''Bullheaded Vagrant:''' What's that got to do with us? Do you think we're the same as those thugs?
:'''Anxious Miner:''' Is anyone with you injured? We have a doctor. She can care for your wounded!
:'''Bullheaded Vagrant:''' Yeah right, and you can guarantee that no one there with you is out for blood? I don't believe it. Stay where you are!
:'''Anxious Miner:''' *sigh* These guys...
{{Dialogue End}}

===Go deep into the mines and help the miners along the way{{subst:void|<!--101050103-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Great Mine|update|On the way deeper into the mines, you can hear the constant screams in the distance. It is obvious that things have gotten pretty serious, you must help the fleeing miners along the way.<br />However, for some reason, you seem to be able to hear the sound of someone snoring...<br />Could it be that you're having hallucinations from the fatigue of travel?}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:'''March 7th:''' That person up ahead... is he asleep?
:'''Seele:''' Let's head up and take a look, he might need help.

;(Talk to Peak)
----
:'''Peak:''' ...
:'''March 7th:''' Falling asleep in a place like this... impressive!
:'''March 7th:''' Hey, wakey-wakey! You'll get mushrooms growing on your head~
----
:<!--0.5-second delay-->
:'''Peak:''' Hm...? Wha...? Mushroom bread...? I can't see it on the menu... Miss Seele?
:'''Seele:''' Have you got a death wish or something? How can you sleep here? Get back to safety and take shelter!
:'''Peak:''' Take shelter... *gasp* I remember now! These guys came out of nowhere and got into a fight with the mining team...
:'''Peak:''' At the time I was exhausted &mdash; I'd hardly run a few feet when one of them caught me. If it weren't for Wildfire, they'd have stolen the clothes off my back!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And then? Where did Wildfire go?
::'''Peak:''' Further in, I guess. Those thugs took control of the vein ages ago &mdash; and they're fully armed. We poor, defenseless, good folks were no match for them.
::'''Peak:''' It's only thanks to Wildfire that the Great Mine hasn't fallen into their hands completely.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...They'd take your clothes? These ones?
::'''Peak:''' You don't know these guys &mdash; no moral compass &mdash; they'd rob you blind in a flash! It's only thanks to Wildfire that the Great Mine hasn't fallen under their control completely.
::'''Peak:''' Uh... speaking of which... where is Wildfire? Did they head further in? Is there a fight happening?
:'''Seele:''' ...It seems like Chief Oleg must be up ahead. Hurry up and get back to safety &mdash; look for Nat. And try not to get into another scrap along the way.
:'''Peak:''' Okay! Thank you for, um... getting me on my feet! If I get back soon enough, I'll have time for a nap...
----
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:'''Seele:''' The giant ore vein &mdash; the one they discovered... That must be where the clashes are centered?
:'''Seele:''' Come on, let's get to higher ground and take a look.
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Great Mine|update|On the way deeper into the mines, you can hear the constant screams in the distance. It is obvious that things have gotten pretty serious, you must help the fleeing miners along the way.<br />You seem to hear a painful moan nearby... Search for it in the vicinity.}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:'''Seele:''' I recognize that woman &mdash; that's Elaine from First Mining Team! Quick, let's get up there and see if she's wounded.

;(Talk to Elaine)
----
:'''Seele:''' Elaine! Are you okay? Are you hurt?
:'''Elaine:''' Seele! Thank goodness. I&mdash;I'm fine, just a couple of sprains.
:'''Elaine:''' You've got good timing &mdash; those vagrants were asking me about the robots, but I don't know anything...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Robots?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Doesn't ring a bell...
:'''Elaine:''' Oh! Don't you know? The inner section of the Great Mine has been seized by a band of robots! Neither the mining team nor the vagrants can get anywhere near.
